From 351d8cc061b302bfd869f44e19732b616bc9703c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <x@x>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:48:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] novo-terminals: follow the core terminal rule; refit pins;
 validate rename and set_level

Core rule (#35):
- Drop the crate's Settings/SameName/JoinLink and the terminals.* info
  properties; read ProjectInfo.rules.terminals (rules()) and change it
  through Command::SetProjectInfo (set_rules()). migrate_legacy_rules()
  moves projects saved with the former property keys onto the typed rule.
- Join: rows group exactly as the netlist joins records (same name and
  level); the NotJoined check is gone. Refuse: place_named no longer makes
  a second record, novo-core's DuplicateTerminal comes back. Off: one row
  per record, duplicates listed as DuplicateName warnings.
- Name-based PE/N recognition now follows rules.potentials
  .from_terminal_names and the project's supply potentials (named_potential,
  kind_for_name(project, name)); the pin-name fallback in place_terminals is
  gone, the netlist potential decides. PotentialKind::Pen maps to a PE
  terminal named PEN; potential_fits accepts PEN only on PE terminals.

Review on 800680b:
- set_kind, set_strip_style and clear_override redraw through redraw(),
  which reads the new symbol's connection points from novo-symbols and
  refits the instance pins; refused when the wire would fold or bend, or
  for a symbol that is not a single-level terminal symbol.
- rename_preview returns RenameChange with a problem (Empty, Taken);
  rename refuses with InvalidValue/AlreadyExists and changes nothing.
- set_level refuses level 0, a (name, level) already on the strip and more
  levels than a multi-level drawing has.

Also: user-facing text in one strings module (rule_sentence is for the
Terminals drawer and the Rules document); explain under Refuse no longer
says only the first drawing counts and no longer builds the whole strip
view; join_duplicates carries jumper, part and properties over; set_jumper
refuses terminals of several strips; strips sort -X2 before -X10; the
screen deduplicates across drawings; next_free_* use a HashSet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DZ68tTULUv7Uhe8ecKbC47
